WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.371 --> 00:00:05.505
GORDON RAMSAY: I
can hear that beast.

00:00:05.572 --> 00:00:06.773
LONELY: Yeah.
GORDON RAMSAY: Yeah.

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:07.574
Loud and clear.

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:12.412
I've been fishing in
some remote places,

00:00:12.479 --> 00:00:15.382
but never in front of
an audience of hippos.

00:00:15.448 --> 00:00:18.017
I'm constantly looking over,
because those things charge.

00:00:18.084 --> 00:00:19.652
Lonely--

00:00:19.719 --> 00:00:20.487
Yes?

00:00:20.553 --> 00:00:22.322
That thing's getting closer.

00:00:22.389 --> 00:00:23.623
Yes, I can see it.

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:24.424
We are safe for now.

00:00:24.491 --> 00:00:25.558
GORDON RAMSAY: Are you sure?

00:00:25.625 --> 00:00:26.393
LONELY: Yes, yes.

00:00:28.495 --> 00:00:30.330
GORDON RAMSAY: Lonely, I'm
three times heavier than you.

00:00:30.397 --> 00:00:31.564
I don't move that quickly.

00:00:31.631 --> 00:00:32.499
Yes.

00:00:32.565 --> 00:00:34.167
I can see they run
faster than you.

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:35.602
GORDON RAMSAY: Trust me.

00:00:35.668 --> 00:00:37.570
I am not leaving here until
I catch a decent fish.

00:00:37.637 --> 00:00:38.972
LONELY: Yes, yes.

00:00:39.038 --> 00:00:40.273
GORDON RAMSAY: Come on, bass.

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:42.542
I'd like to catch
a [bleep] fish.

00:00:42.609 --> 00:00:44.577
Come on.

00:00:44.644 --> 00:00:45.412
Oh.

00:00:45.478 --> 00:00:46.246
I think I've got one.

00:00:46.312 --> 00:00:47.814
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:00:47.881 --> 00:00:49.082
No.
No I haven't.

00:00:49.149 --> 00:00:50.183
- You missed it.
- No, no.

00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:51.351
He's on.
LONELY: Still on.

00:00:51.418 --> 00:00:52.318
GORDON RAMSAY: He's still on.

00:00:52.385 --> 00:00:53.353
LONELY: Yes, yes.

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:55.722
Pull it back slowly, slowly.

00:00:55.789 --> 00:00:56.790
Good.
Oh.

00:00:56.856 --> 00:00:57.624
Good.

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:59.692
You see?

00:00:59.759 --> 00:01:01.861
GORDON RAMSAY: Now that
is a good one for the--

00:01:01.928 --> 00:01:03.062
- For the chief.
- For the chief.

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:04.097
Right.

00:01:05.532 --> 00:01:07.967
GORDON RAMSAY: Now Lonely may
have caught the most fish,

00:01:08.034 --> 00:01:09.102
but let's be honest.

00:01:09.169 --> 00:01:11.271
I caught the biggest.

00:01:11.337 --> 00:01:13.573
I want to save my
fish for the chief.

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:16.242
So I'm taking one of
Lonely's back to Zola.

00:01:16.309 --> 00:01:17.844
She might assume
that I caught it.

00:01:17.911 --> 00:01:20.880
But if you don't say
anything, I won't either.

00:01:20.947 --> 00:01:21.714
Zola.

00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:23.016
Hey!

00:01:23.082 --> 00:01:24.284
We are not empty-handed.

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:25.785
Oh, look at that.

00:01:25.852 --> 00:01:27.921
I'd like you to scale and
gut that guy for me, please.

00:01:27.987 --> 00:01:29.155
GORDON RAMSAY: Scale and gut it.

00:01:29.222 --> 00:01:30.590
ZOLA NENE: The point
here for the week

00:01:30.657 --> 00:01:33.226
is to hone your Zulu
warriors skills.

00:01:33.293 --> 00:01:34.427
GORDON RAMSAY: Right.

00:01:34.494 --> 00:01:36.463
ZOLA NENE: Braaing
is quintessential.

00:01:36.529 --> 00:01:38.498
We're keeping it very
plain, very simple,

00:01:38.565 --> 00:01:39.899
just a little bit of seasoning.

00:01:39.966 --> 00:01:41.768
The ingredients speak for
themselves, generally.

00:01:41.835 --> 00:01:43.002
GORDON RAMSAY: Yeah.

00:01:43.069 --> 00:01:44.604
ZOLA NENE: Which is,
you know, in line

00:01:44.671 --> 00:01:47.106
with tradition, in terms of our
flavor profile of Zulu people.

00:01:47.173 --> 00:01:48.475
GORDON RAMSAY: Gotcha.

00:01:48.541 --> 00:01:52.111
So here I'm making
something called ushatini.

00:01:52.178 --> 00:01:55.448
It's a combination of
onions and tomatoes,

00:01:55.515 --> 00:01:57.150
chopped up, which I've got here.

00:01:57.217 --> 00:01:58.585
And I've been mentioning
to you how, you know,

00:01:58.651 --> 00:02:00.720
the Zulu palate is
very simplistic.

00:02:00.787 --> 00:02:02.121
GORDON RAMSAY: Yeah.

00:02:02.188 --> 00:02:05.158
ZOLA NENE: But KZN is
the biggest population of

00:02:05.225 --> 00:02:07.360
Indian people outside of India.

00:02:07.427 --> 00:02:09.996
We do add a touch of
chili every now and then.

00:02:10.063 --> 00:02:11.331
Right.

00:02:11.397 --> 00:02:12.999
Because that sort of
culture has infiltrated

00:02:13.066 --> 00:02:14.868
throughout the region.

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:16.102
GORDON RAMSAY: So no oil?

00:02:16.169 --> 00:02:16.970
ZOLA NENE: No oil.

00:02:17.036 --> 00:02:18.238
No, no oil.

00:02:18.304 --> 00:02:19.806
Remember, this is
Zulu warrior cooking.

00:02:19.873 --> 00:02:21.374
Sure.

00:02:21.441 --> 00:02:23.309
There was no such thing as
olive oil available, et cetera.

00:02:23.376 --> 00:02:25.144
So you just went
straight on to the fire.

00:02:25.211 --> 00:02:26.446
- Straight on?
- On to the fire.

00:02:26.513 --> 00:02:27.580
Yeah.

00:02:27.647 --> 00:02:28.681
So wherever you see the
coals at their whitest--

00:02:28.748 --> 00:02:29.916
GORDON RAMSAY: There.

00:02:29.983 --> 00:02:31.184
--you'll know that they're
the right temperature.

00:02:31.251 --> 00:02:32.018
There you go.

00:02:32.085 --> 00:02:33.786
Good sizzle.

00:02:33.853 --> 00:02:35.288
Wow.

00:02:35.355 --> 00:02:36.756
What's becoming very obvious
is that it's very simple--

00:02:36.823 --> 00:02:38.324
That's it.

00:02:38.391 --> 00:02:40.994
--this tribal cooking, in a
way that it's a huge emphasis

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:42.161
on the fish and the meat.

00:02:42.228 --> 00:02:43.363
ZOLA NENE: Yes.

00:02:43.429 --> 00:02:44.964
What's the big
no-nos for the chief?

00:02:45.031 --> 00:02:48.902
Zulu people in general do
not like their meat rare.

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:50.203
I know--
- Damn.

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:51.271
--you know, you're
Gordon, so you're going

00:02:51.337 --> 00:02:52.038
to want to give them--
- Damn.

00:02:52.105 --> 00:02:53.373
--medium raw.

00:02:53.439 --> 00:02:54.641
What would happen if
you just try and suggest

00:02:54.707 --> 00:02:55.842
he takes it medium rare?

00:02:55.909 --> 00:02:57.443
I don't know.

00:02:57.510 --> 00:03:00.346
I've never heard anyone suggest
anything to the chief before.

00:03:00.413 --> 00:03:02.248
But you could be
the first, Gordon.

00:03:02.315 --> 00:03:03.550
GORDON RAMSAY: Beautiful.

00:03:03.616 --> 00:03:05.218
ZOLA NENE: Beautiful,
fresh piece of fish.

00:03:05.285 --> 00:03:06.452
GORDON RAMSAY: Wow.

00:03:06.519 --> 00:03:07.587
ZOLA NENE: Right on there.
- Oh my god.

00:03:07.654 --> 00:03:09.355
ZOLA NENE: Hang
onto that for me.

00:03:09.422 --> 00:03:12.058
And then I'm going to pop the
shatini on top of the flesh.

00:03:12.125 --> 00:03:13.326
GORDON RAMSAY: Amazing
how simple it is.

00:03:13.393 --> 00:03:15.161
And you think of
the fierce warrior,

00:03:15.228 --> 00:03:18.431
in terms of what he stands
for, how important he is,

00:03:18.498 --> 00:03:19.632
and look how simple that is.

00:03:19.699 --> 00:03:20.433
That's it, simple.

00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:25.138
Delicious.

00:03:25.204 --> 00:03:26.306
Good fishing.
GORDON RAMSAY: That's delicious.

00:03:26.372 --> 00:03:27.507
ZOLA NENE: Hmm.
So good.

00:03:27.574 --> 00:03:29.008
So good.
GORDON RAMSAY: But so simple.

00:03:29.075 --> 00:03:30.343
ZOLA NENE: So simple.

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:32.712
All the ingredients
speak for themselves.

00:03:32.779 --> 00:03:34.647
I will see you--
I'll see at the end of the week.

00:03:34.714 --> 00:03:35.515
At the end of the week.

00:03:35.582 --> 00:03:36.716
Any tips?

00:03:36.783 --> 00:03:38.284
Mostly listen and learn.

00:03:38.351 --> 00:03:39.819
GORDON RAMSAY: Right.

00:03:39.886 --> 00:03:42.822
And always remember, the
chief is a hard man to please.

00:03:42.889 --> 00:03:43.656
- Gotcha.
- Good luck.

00:03:43.723 --> 00:03:44.457
Thank you.

00:03:44.524 --> 00:03:45.925
It sounds like I'll need it.

00:03:45.992 --> 00:03:47.694
[laughing]

